<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahdist War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1881–1899</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mahdist War was fought from 1881 to 1899 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> between the followers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ahmad">Muhammad Ahmad</a>, who proclaimed himself the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a>, and the Egyptian government backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. The Mahdists took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khartoum">Khartoum</a> in 1885, killing Charles Gordon, and built their own state, which an Anglo-Egyptian army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herbert-kitchener">Herbert Kitchener</a> destroyed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omdurman">Omdurman</a> in 1898.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahdist-war.jpg" alt="Mahdist War" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fidodog14 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahdist_War_Collage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
